5. AI Development Strategy

Artificial Intelligence will be used as a development accelerator.

AI will assist in:

UI Development
Boilerplate Code
Refactoring
Documentation
Testing
Debugging

Product decisions will always remain human-driven.

6. Git Strategy

Every feature should have its own branch.

Commits should be meaningful.

Example:

Setup backend

Add subject CRUD

Implement progress tracking

Build admin dashboard

Avoid large commits containing unrelated changes.

7. Coding Standards
Clean Code
Reusable Components
Feature-based Architecture
Proper Naming
Small Functions
Modular Design
Meaningful Comments
Consistent Formatting
8. Testing Strategy

Every completed feature should be tested before moving to the next phase.

Testing includes:

Functional Testing
UI Testing
API Testing
Database Testing
Responsive Testing

No unfinished feature should move to production.

9. Deployment Strategy

Development Environment

↓

Testing Environment

↓

Production Environment

Production deployment should happen only after successful testing.

10. MVP Completion Checklist

The MVP will be considered complete when:

Admin Login works
Student Dashboard works
Subject Management works
Chapter Management works
Resource Management works
File Upload works
Progress Tracking works
Analytics work
Search works
Responsive UI works
Platform is deployed successfully
11. Success Metrics

The first version of PrepFlow should achieve:

Fast loading experience
Clean UI
Easy navigation
Organized learning
Zero code content management
Reliable progress tracking
12. Long-Term Goal

PrepFlow should evolve into a complete preparation ecosystem where students can:

Learn
Organize
Track
Revise
Compete
Improve

using a single platform.

13. Final Development Principles

Build the foundation before features.

Keep everything dynamic.

Never hardcode content.

Never compromise maintainability for speed.

Design for future expansion.

Always prioritize user experience.

14. Final Statement

PrepFlow is not just another educational project.

It is a long-term platform designed to simplify preparation through structured learning, powerful content management, and an exceptional user experience.

Every phase of development should contribute toward building a scalable, maintainable, and student-first ecosystem.